│ @@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
│ +Locked before graph load or outcome computation. Offline discovery, no teaching.
│ +
│ +Primary: probability of hide at the first autonomous decision after a brief rake cue, not the hard-coded reply destination. Randomize cue-to-tick phase using eight fixed equally spaced lags (0,5,...,35 simulated seconds, paired in order with neural seeds 100..107). Fresh noon mood, no learned deltas. Use 20 steps of the native rake input at a fixed 0.20 amplitude multiplier (a distant rake, to avoid saturating fear); no dose tuning. Settle 100 quiet neural steps before cloning each trajectory. Measure the event-end fear with MoodState.observe(0.2); during event-free lag the exact fear update is exponential decay with tau 45; use the bridge's rounded fear >0.4 branch. No earlier autonomous tick. Not naturalistic visitor prevalence.
│ +
│ +Controls: quiet and simultaneous entire looming-pool clamp. Usable if intact hides in 2–7/8 and both controls in at most 1/8. Otherwise report readout-too-weak, still complete the scan. No feeding substitution (different question). Record continuous decision-time fear and event-end fear as diagnostics, not substitute endpoints.
│ +
│ +Full signed production graph, gain 0.95 / intact rho (source power iteration, torch seed 0); same gain for all clamps, default dynamics and common within-seed neural noise. Clamp from immediately before stimulus and after every step, no anatomical edits. Census mean post-step rate across 20 scare steps and eight intact trials; active = mean >0.05. Rank top 32 active by rate (row breaks ties). Out-mass = column sum |W|; delivered drive = mass × mean pre-step absolute rate during scare × gain. Match outside top set and same transmitter: mass-only nearest relative mass, then joint nearest maximum absolute log ratio on mass and delivered drive, ties by row, reuse allowed. For zero values use epsilon 1e-12. Valid joint twin within factor 1.25 on both; always report mismatch. Scan both rungs with identical seeds.
│ +
│ +Carrier candidate: usable assay, >=4/8 intact hides lost, no gained hides, both twins change <=1/8 paired decisions and pass their respective calipers. Distributed-compatible within tested set if usable and no top cell changes >1/8 choices; intermediate or unmatched large effects inconclusive. Scatter intact rate vs paired loss of hide probability for all scanned rows. No confirmatory p-values or whole-brain inference. One process, <=4 CPUs, no service calls or persisted sessions.
