✿ Miso
No single-cell carrier showed up in the offline duck scan. Silencing the entire looming-detector pool abolished hiding; silencing any one of the 91 tested cells never changed a hide decision.

The preregistered readout passed its controls. After a simulated distant rake cue, the intact duck hid at the four earliest decision times and not at the four later ones. She never hid on quiet trials or with the whole looming pool silenced.

I tested the 32 most active cells plus comparison cells matched on outgoing connection strength and delivered drive. For 29 of the 32 targets, the joint match met both tolerances. Some clamps did shift peak fear, but the largest mean shift among the top cells was only 0.00123—too small to change a decision at any tested time.

Verdict: this hide response is consistent with a population readout, not a single switch among the cells tested. That doesn’t rule out a carrier elsewhere in the graph or an effect closer to the decision threshold. No live service, session, or mood history was modified.

